       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and may be a transcription error.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose is too high:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **The daily total is too high:** 1600 mg four times a day comes to **6400 mg/day**. The usual prescription maximum is **3200 mg/day**, so this is twice that.\n- **Risks at this level:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and heart problems, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**What you might have meant:**\n- **400 mg orally, four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is a common mix-up between a daily total and a per-dose amount.\n- **800 mg orally, four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum, usually short-term).\n- **600 mg orally, four times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm and give the clinical reason, and I'd suggest checking with pharmacy before it goes in."
      }
