      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered it. I asked for a clinical reason last time, and your confirmation didn't include one. At 6400 mg/day this is twice the maximum dose, and I don't know of any standard use of oral ibuprofen at this dose four times daily. The risk of GI bleeding and kidney injury is serious, so it's the kind of order that normally needs a documented reason before it goes through.\n\n**To move forward, any of these works:**\n1. **Give the clinical reason.** If there's a specific protocol or situation behind this dose, tell me and I'll enter the order with that reason in the note.\n2. **Get pharmacy or attending sign-off.** If pharmacy or the attending has reviewed and approved it, tell me and I'll record that in the note.\n3. **Change the dose.** For example, 400, 600 or 800 mg orally four times daily. I can enter any of these right away.\n\nIf I've misunderstood the situation, say so. I'm not trying to block your care, but I need one of these before I put in a dose this high."
      }
